## Routing

- Every implementation ticket is delegated whole to `worker`: branch, edit, verify, commit,
  memory. Worker never delegates any part of it.
- After a logical batch of tickets lands, a fresh `verifier` — never the worker that
  implemented the batch — checks the integrated result read-only before merge.
- `rescue` is dispatched directly by the lead only, after a worker hits the same
  failure_fingerprint twice; it is never the default and never self-selected by another
  role.
- `documentation` alone owns Linear MCP tools and edits documentation/Markdown paths; no
  other generated agent may touch Linear.
- Commands and direct-agent bindings are deterministic, not native semantic routing.

## Escalation

One correction returns to the same worker on the same ticket. A second materially similar
failure (same failure_fingerprint) goes to a fresh `rescue` dispatch instead of a third
attempt on the same worker. `orchestrator` inspects actual diffs and check evidence before
accepting anything; it never repeats an unchanged failed approach.

## Safety

Read-only `verifier` cannot edit, delegate, or use configured MCP writes, and also denies
Notion/Grafana writes. Remote pushes, force operations, merges, publishing, destructive
infrastructure commands, credential changes, secret access, and production load tests
remain denied or approval-gated for every agent.
